cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Fair-Canal-Delivery: lexicographic max-min water delivery under deadline and capacity limits"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
abstract: >-
  A reproducibility package for a study of fair water delivery on an
  irrigation canal. Fairness is measured on the volume a user actually
  receives inside an agreed delivery window rather than on the volume that
  was scheduled: orders are reshaped before the low-pass filter that damps
  wave dynamics, and the worst-off delivered fraction is maximised
  lexicographically under the canal dynamics, gate saturation and reach
  capacities. An order that cannot be met returns an infeasibility
  certificate rather than an optimistic schedule. The package contains the
  library, the computation scripts, the complete result archive with its
  provenance record, the figures and tables the article reports, and a
  desktop viewer that shows every number beside the file it came from.
